    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, we're having an issue with our sublimation heat presses. the ink isn't transferring fully onto the polyester fabric, leaving these patchy, faded spots in the print. we're running at 200c for 40 seconds with about 4 bar of pressure. any idea why the color transfer is failing?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Patchy transfers with sublimation ink on polyester fabric are usually a sign that the heat or pressure isn't quite right for the specific ink or material combination. It's often a matter of temperature calibration, or perhaps the heat press plate itself is not reaching a consistent, even heat across the entire surface. You might need to experiment with increasing the temperature slightly, perhaps up to 205°C, or extending the time to 45 seconds. Remember, the material's specific sublimation temperature is key, and sometimes the ink requires a little more time to fully bond with the polyester fibers.",
      "source": "target",
