    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "we checked the heat distribution with a thermal camera and the plates are actually coming out even. pressure seems consistent too. it's just weird because some parts look perfect and then a few inches away it's just... gone. like the color just vanished or didn't make it into the fabric at all. could it be an issue with the humidity in the factory or something in the ink itself?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the heat and pressure are verified as consistent, then the issue might indeed be related to the environment or the ink itself. Humidity can play a minor role, though it's less common for such localized failures unless the ink formulation is particularly sensitive. I'd suggest checking the ink batch for any signs of contamination or expiration, as even a slight degradation in the pigment quality can cause inconsistent transfer. It's also worth ensuring the sublimation paper is clean and properly primed, as a greasy surface can repel the ink transfer process.",
      "source": "target",
